   "text": "internals \u00b7 _run_guarded(client, query, log, run)",
   "originalText": "internals \u00b7 _run_guarded(client, query, log, run)",
   "fontSize": 20,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.15,
   "autoResize": true
  },
  {
   "id": "t-89",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 56,
   "y": 1567.6,
   "width": 888,
   "height": 252.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [
    "g-86"
   ],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 1083438815,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1492026738,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "1. client.query(query, dry_run=True)  \u2192 dry\n2. dry.statement_type == 'SELECT'    else [{ error: 'Only a single SELECT statement is allowed.' }]\n3. referenced tables within allowed_tables()    (the 15 current_* views plus the tables they read; built\nonce by dry-running SELECT * on each view)\n   else [{ error: 'Only these views may be queried: [...]' }]\n4. log.append(query)                  \u2192 answer.queries\n5. client.query(query, maximum_bytes_billed = 1_000_000_000)\n   job.result(max_results = 200)      (1 GB cap; over it \u2192 BadRequest \u2192 [{ error }])\n6. run.bytes_billed = job.total_bytes_billed;   json_rows(rows) makes them JSON-safe\n\nEvery view reads precomputed counters, so a typical question bills kilobytes.\nViews: current_champion_stats, _trait_stats, _item_stats, _champion_item_stats / _pair_ / _trio_,\n_composition_stats, _composition_variant_stats, _composition_star_upgrade_stats,\n_composition_completed_item_stats, _composition_board_cost_stats, _composition_unit_stats,\n_composition_trait_stats, _matches, _participant_compositions",
   "originalText": "1. client.query(query, dry_run=True)  \u2192 dry\n2. dry.statement_type == 'SELECT'    else [{ error: 'Only a single SELECT statement is allowed.' }]\n3. referenced tables within allowed_tables()    (the 15 current_* views plus the tables they read; built\nonce by dry-running SELECT * on each view)\n   else [{ error: 'Only these views may be queried: [...]' }]\n4. log.append(query)                  \u2192 answer.queries\n5. client.query(query, maximum_bytes_billed = 1_000_000_000)\n   job.result(max_results = 200)      (1 GB cap; over it \u2192 BadRequest \u2192 [{ error }])\n6. run.bytes_billed = job.total_bytes_billed;   json_rows(rows) makes them JSON-safe\n\nEvery view reads precomputed counters, so a typical question bills kilobytes.\nViews: current_champion_stats, _trait_stats, _item_stats, _champion_item_stats / _pair_ / _trio_,\n_composition_stats, _composition_variant_stats, _composition_star_upgrade_stats,\n_composition_completed_item_stats, _composition_board_cost_stats, _composition_unit_stats,\n_composition_trait_stats, _matches, _participant_compositions",
   "fontSize": 14,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.2,
   "autoResize": true
  },
