   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "_roll_odds\n \u2022 UnitNeed / TierOut .model_validate (pydantic; a bad shape is a ValueError \u2192 { error })\n \u2022 unit_costs(client): cached  SELECT name, cost FROM current_champion_stats  \u2192 { normalised_name: \n   (name, cost) }\n   unknown name \u2192 ValueError('Unknown unit(s): ... Use these names: ...')\n \u2022 targets = [ RollTarget(name, cost, copies, copies_out) ];  tier_out folded into { cost: copies_gone\n    }\ncalculate_roll_odds(level, targets, gold or DEFAULT_GOLD, gone_by_cost)\n \u2022 validate(): level 2-11, cost 1-5, copies >= 1, states = product of(copies+1) <= 200 000, gold 0..300\n \u2022 dist = np.zeros(shape = (copies_1+1, ..., copies_n+1))   P(k_1...k_n copies bought so far);  dist[0,...,0] = \n   1\n \u2022 slot_odds(): per cell, P(one shop slot shows unit i) = SHOP_ODDS_PER_LEVEL[level][cost] \u00d7 unit_left\n    / cost_left\n   (same-cost units share one pool, so their cost_left depends on every unit's progress); stay = 1 - sum of\n    hits\n \u2022 one Roll = 5 \u00d7 step_slot(dist, hit_odds, stay);   snapshot(dist) after every Roll\n \u2022 spend = sum of cost \u00d7 copies  (buys the copies first);  Rolls at gold g = (g - spend) // 2\n \u2022 keep rolling until all_units >= 95 %, covering >= 100 gold and every asked amount, capped at 300 gold\n \u2022 snapshot.all_units = dist[goal];  per_unit[name] = marginal(dist, axis, copies)",
   "originalText": "_roll_odds\n \u2022 UnitNeed / TierOut .model_validate (pydantic; a bad shape is a ValueError \u2192 { error })\n \u2022 unit_costs(client): cached  SELECT name, cost FROM current_champion_stats  \u2192 { normalised_name: \n   (name, cost) }\n   unknown name \u2192 ValueError('Unknown unit(s): ... Use these names: ...')\n \u2022 targets = [ RollTarget(name, cost, copies, copies_out) ];  tier_out folded into { cost: copies_gone\n    }\ncalculate_roll_odds(level, targets, gold or DEFAULT_GOLD, gone_by_cost)\n \u2022 validate(): level 2-11, cost 1-5, copies >= 1, states = product of(copies+1) <= 200 000, gold 0..300\n \u2022 dist = np.zeros(shape = (copies_1+1, ..., copies_n+1))   P(k_1...k_n copies bought so far);  dist[0,...,0] = \n   1\n \u2022 slot_odds(): per cell, P(one shop slot shows unit i) = SHOP_ODDS_PER_LEVEL[level][cost] \u00d7 unit_left\n    / cost_left\n   (same-cost units share one pool, so their cost_left depends on every unit's progress); stay = 1 - sum of\n    hits\n \u2022 one Roll = 5 \u00d7 step_slot(dist, hit_odds, stay);   snapshot(dist) after every Roll\n \u2022 spend = sum of cost \u00d7 copies  (buys the copies first);  Rolls at gold g = (g - spend) // 2\n \u2022 keep rolling until all_units >= 95 %, covering >= 100 gold and every asked amount, capped at 300 gold\n \u2022 snapshot.all_units = dist[goal];  per_unit[name] = marginal(dist, axis, copies)",
